{"kind":"grammar","lang":"en","entities":{"n5-908":{"renderings":[{"id":"fcfc5ac22f2a9afb","role":"label","field":"name","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-908"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Plain negative"},{"id":"82c55b1e7909e43b","role":"prose","field":"shortExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-908"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"The plain negative of an い-adjective."},{"id":"49081810831dae23","role":"prose","field":"longExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-908"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"い-adjectives inflect themselves: the negative replaces い with くない. Only いい/良い is irregular, using the よ- stem (よくない)."},{"id":"405a3443ba643b2c","role":"prose","field":"formation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-908"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Drop the final い and add くない: 高い -> 高くない. Irregular: いい -> よくない."},{"id":"b710f51df768f9fd","role":"label","field":"derives","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n5-908"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"negative (くない)"}]}}}